    <statement><p>Consider the shaded region in the graph below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap16Sec2__Q17__pg-image-1.png" width="41%"/>
<p>Write <m>\int_R f\,dA</m> on this region as an iterated integral:</p>
<p><m>\int_R f\,dA = \int_a^b\int_c^d f(x,y)\, d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/>
where</p>
<p><m>a =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/>,</p>
<p><m>b =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/>,</p>
<p><m>c =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/>, and</p>
<p><m>d =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\mathopen{}\left(x-2\right)}{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(2,0)</m> and
<m>(6,2)</m> is
<me>y = \frac{1}{2}(x - 2).</me>
So the integral is
<me>\int_{2}^{6} \int_{\frac{1}{2}(x - 2)}^{3} f(x,y) \,dy\,dx.</me>
Note that for this region it is not possible to write <m>\int_R\,f\,dA</m>
as a single integral with <m>dA = dx\,dy</m>.



</solution>
